  "notes": "{清書|せいしょ} refers to the final, neat version of a handwritten document. Before word processors, making a {清書|せいしょ} was an important step in producing formal documents.\n\nPROCESS:\n1. {下書|したが}き: rough draft\n2. {清書|せいしょ}: clean/fair copy\n\nCOMMON CONTEXTS:\n- School assignments (writing out final copies)\n- Calligraphy ({習字|しゅうじ}/{書道|しょどう})\n- Formal documents\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {下書|したが}き: rough draft, preliminary version\n- {原稿|げんこう}: manuscript",
